## 3. Create Jenkins Agent User and SSH Keys

Create the user:

```bash
useradd devopsadmin -s /bin/bash -m -d /home/devopsadmin

su - devopsadmin
```

Generate SSH keys:

```bash
ssh-keygen -t ecdsa -b 521
```

Check the generated keys:

```bash
ls ~/.ssh
```

The directory should contain:

```text
id_ecdsa
id_ecdsa.pub
```

* `id_ecdsa` → Private Key
* `id_ecdsa.pub` → Public Key

Configure the public key for SSH authentication:

```bash
cat ~/.ssh/id_ecdsa.pub > ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

chmod 600 ~/.ssh/*
```

---

# 4. Attach Jenkins Agent Node to Jenkins Controller

Login to Jenkins:

```text
Manage Jenkins
    ↓
Nodes
    ↓
New Node
    ↓
Enter Node Name
    ↓
Select Permanent Agent
```

Configure the SSH connection parameters:

* Node Name
* Host Name
* User Name
* Credentials
* SSH connection details

The Jenkins Controller will use SSH to connect to the Jenkins Agent and execute application builds.

