# 5. Install Apache Tomcat Application Server

Launch a new Ubuntu 24.04 EC2 instance.

Allow TCP port `8080` in the Security Group.

Refer to the official Tomcat documentation:

[Apache Tomcat](https://tomcat.apache.org/?utm_source=chatgpt.com)

### Install Java

```bash
sudo -i

apt update -y

apt-get install default-jdk -y

java --version
```

### Download and Install Tomcat

```bash
cd /opt

wget https://archive.apache.org/dist/tomcat/tomcat-8/v8.5.99/bin/apache-tomcat-8.5.99.tar.gz

tar -xvzf apache-tomcat-8.5.99.tar.gz

mv apache-tomcat-8.5.99 tomcat
```

Start Tomcat:

```bash
cd /opt/tomcat/bin

./startup.sh
```

Access Tomcat:

```text
http://<Public_IP_Address>:8080/
```

---

# 6. Configure SSH Access to Tomcat Server

Create the deployment user:

```bash
useradd devopsadmin -s /bin/bash -m -d /home/devopsadmin

su - devopsadmin
```

Generate SSH keys:

```bash
ssh-keygen -t ecdsa -b 521
```

Configure the public key:

```bash
cat ~/.ssh/id_ecdsa.pub > ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

chmod 600 ~/.ssh/*
```

Give the deployment user ownership of the Tomcat directory:

```bash
chown -R devopsadmin /opt/tomcat
```

---

# 7. Configure Jenkins for Artifact Deployment

The **Publish Over SSH** plugin can be used to copy application artifacts from the Jenkins Agent to the Tomcat Server.

Install the plugin from:

```text
Jenkins
    ↓
Manage Jenkins
    ↓
Plugins
    ↓
Available Plugins
    ↓
Publish Over SSH
```

Configure the Tomcat Server connection in Jenkins and use it in the CI/CD pipeline to deploy the generated `.war` artifact.

## Deployment Flow

```text
Developer
    ↓
Git Repository
    ↓
Jenkins Controller
    ↓
Jenkins Agent
    ↓
Maven Build
    ↓
*.war
    ↓
Publish Over SSH
    ↓
Tomcat Server
    ↓
/opt/tomcat/webapps/
```
